{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Rule base stays proven",
  "description": "Kiro IDE hook: when the Prolog rule base, the prover or the rule text is edited, ask the agent to keep every answer provable and cited, and to cover each new rule with a test.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": ["src/logic/**/*.pl", "src/logic/rules.ts"]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "The rule base, prover or rule text changed. Check that every rule id has plain-English text in src/logic/rules.ts (with an answer sentence if its head is verdict/2), that no topic can prove both yes and no, and that lease facts stay closed-world (absent/1 only when no clause states the fact). Add a row to the matrix in tests/unit/rulebase.test.ts for each new verdict rule, then run `npm test` and fix the code, not the test, unless requirements in .kiro/specs/proof-chain-answers/requirements.md say the test is wrong."
  }
}
